---
title: Pan-Seared Duck Breast Appetizer
servings: 4
description: Tally Ho Supper Club, Hayward, WI
source: Wisconsin Supper Clubs Cookbook
tags: Appetizer, Duck, Want to Try
---

= Vinaigrette =
In a #small bowl{}, combine @sun-dried sour cherries{2%tbsp}, @shallots{1%tbsp}(minced),
@red wine vinegar{3%tbsp}, @toasted sesame oil{1/2%cup}, @salt, and @pepper. 
Set aside.

= Duck =
Preheat oven to 375°F.
Use a sharp knife to score the @duck breasts{4}(boneless, 6oz each), skin side up.
Season with @kosher salt{} and @pepper.

Preheat an #ovenproof skillet{} over medium-high heat, then add the @toasted sesame oil{2%tbsp}.
Use tongs to gently add duck breasts, skin side down.
Sear ~{5%minutes}, or until skin is browned and crispy.

Place skillet in oven for ~{5%minutes} or until cooked to medium.
Remove skillet and let duck breasts rest for ~{5%minutes} while setting up plates. 

= Serving =
Line each salad plate with a handful of @salad greens{}.
Top with sliced duck, fanned out.

Garnish with @sour cherries{}, @raspberries{}(fresh), and @mint{}(fresh). 
Drizzle with 1/4 cup vinaigrette.
